cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this repository and the accompanying manuscript when using the benchmark."
title: "Coalition Deception and Defensive Adaptation in a Social-Deduction Benchmark"
type: software
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-11"
authors:
  - family-names: "Lin"
    given-names: "Isaac"
  - family-names: "Chen"
    given-names: "Xi"
repository-code: "https://github.com/IsaacLin247/coalition-deception"
url: "https://github.com/IsaacLin247/coalition-deception"
abstract: >-
  A social-deduction benchmark with completed corrected experiments on coalition
  deception, defensive adaptation, and repeated response learning. The package
  includes code, protocols, final seed-level analysis, manuscript and versioned
  access to raw data and checkpoints. It distinguishes coalition victory,
  innocent ejections, and mechanisms under adaptive attacks.
keywords:
  - multi-agent reinforcement learning
  - social deduction
  - coalition deception
license: MIT
